WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.150
- [Narrator] Burträsk, Northern Sweden,

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.790
a small village where you can get lit

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.480
by magical lights at night.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.600
And during the day,

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.120
you can worry about their great mystery.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.410
Yeah, somewhere between that house

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.333
and these cute reindeer and
this giant row of trees,

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:17.800
there is a Century-old enigma involving,

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.440
cheese.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.863
Yep, this big ball of cheese.

00:00:22.863 --> 00:00:25.863
(suspenseful music)

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.650
Well, as for all mystery tales

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.750
a star storyteller is essential,

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.023
and today, that is Thomas Rudin,

00:00:36.685 --> 00:00:38.620
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.260
- Västerbottensost is the
emperor of Swedish cheeses.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.150
I've been making

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.813
the Västerbottensost nearly 40 years now.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.231
It was invented long time ago

00:00:49.231 --> 00:00:51.880
back in 1872.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:55.460
The maturation is at least 14 month

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.450
because a good cheese will take its time.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:01.525
It's a very unique taste.
- It has a bitter

00:01:01.525 --> 00:01:03.620
and milky flavor, and oh do

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.020
the Swedes love it.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:07.460
They put it on basically everything.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.920
But for some reason it
can't be made anywhere else

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:10.753
in the world,

00:01:10.753 --> 00:01:12.451
aside from this one factory.

00:01:12.451 --> 00:01:15.483
It's one of Sweden's greatest mysteries.

00:01:17.416 --> 00:01:18.960
- We have tried to make it

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.130
in Falkenburg down in south of Sweden

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.360
also tried to make it in Bollnäs

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.050
and also in Åmål.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:28.090
But it hasn't been the
real Västerbotten cheese.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:31.309
We don't get the unique
taste and flavor of it.

00:01:31.309 --> 00:01:32.904
- [Narrator] And, why?

00:01:32.904 --> 00:01:34.218
No one really knows.

00:01:34.218 --> 00:01:36.810
Some blame it on a meteor that struck

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.300
the village some 20,000 years ago,

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.050
which created this lake

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.340
and, in turn, enriched
the soil with calcium,

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:45.000
which affects the cows in the region,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.908
which affects the milk
and cheese they produce.

00:01:47.908 --> 00:01:48.876
- [Group] Ah.

00:01:48.876 --> 00:01:50.900
- [Narrator] Another theory
suggests the cheese's

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.440
unique flavor is influenced

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.740
by the bacteria in the air

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.326
of the old factory building.

00:01:55.326 --> 00:01:56.159
- [Group] Oo.

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:58.987
- [Narrator] I mean the air is so precious

00:01:58.987 --> 00:02:00.810
to the cheese's flavor that
when the building expanded,

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:01.930
holes were made so that the air

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.430
from the old building would
flow into the new one.

00:02:06.018 --> 00:02:08.009
- There is a combination with

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:11.260
the kind of milk that
we're using from the cows

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.337
in our region combined with the microflora

00:02:14.337 --> 00:02:16.204
in our dairy.

00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:19.565
If we call that magic or not,

00:02:19.565 --> 00:02:20.813
OK.

00:02:20.813 --> 00:02:22.830
- [Narrator] One thing is certain,

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:24.700
this magic cheese is kept alive

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.938
by the people working on it.

00:02:25.938 --> 00:02:28.266
- [Thomas] I feel very humble for the fact

00:02:28.266 --> 00:02:30.794
that I'm allowed to work with this cheese.

00:02:30.794 --> 00:02:34.497
It's a bit of the mystery
that's why it's special.

00:02:34.497 --> 00:02:35.900
- [Narrator] Last thing,

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:37.333
can you give us the recipe?

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:42.650
- No because that's the big
secret with this cheese.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:46.313
- [Narrator] Hm, mystery solved, maybe.

00:02:47.635 --> 00:02:48.963
- Goodnight,

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.304
goodnight.

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:54.887
(upbeat music)

